; The claim tron-rpc-grpc makes is that gRPC reaches the same places HTTP does
; -- a Solo5 vsock included. This target is that claim, checked.
;
; It instantiates the client over a flow that is not a socket at all, and names
; no Unix package. If Io_of_flow ever needs something only a real file
; descriptor has, or if h2's closure acquires unix, this stops linking.
;
; Deliberately not a Solo5 image. Cross-compiling is a separate exercise with
; its own open question about GMP -- see ../../docs/unikernel.md. This answers
; the part that can be answered on every runner, on every commit.

(executable
 (name grpc_flow_link)
 (libraries tron-types tron-rpc tron-rpc-grpc lwt cstruct mirage-flow fmt))
